<!--
Furniture Locator - Keybind definition

This file MUST be named exactly "bindings.xml" -- that's a hard
requirement of the addon keybind system, confirmed against several
real working addons (ESO-MailLooter, ESO-RaidNotifier) that all use
this exact filename.

Attaching to the built-in "SI_KEYBINDINGS_LAYER_GENERAL" layer (the
same layer other simple addon keybinds use) means this shows up under
Controls > Keybindings and works any time, without needing any custom
action-layer push/pop logic of our own.

FIX: this used to call SCENE_MANAGER:Toggle("FurnitureLocatorSceneGamepad")
directly, which shows the bare item-list screen with no category/style
selected yet. Since every item resolves to a real category (falling back
to "Uncategorized", never nil), a nil currentCategory filter matches
zero items -- so the very first time this keybind was pressed in a
session, it showed a blank list (just "< Back" rows), looking broken.
Routing through FurnitureLocatorDialogs.ShowCategoryDialog() (v13: opens Home) -- the same
entry point the Quickslot Wheel slot and /flocator2 already use -- keeps
this keybind consistent with the rest of the addon's real flow.
-->
<Bindings>
    <Layer name="SI_KEYBINDINGS_LAYER_GENERAL">
        <Category name="Furniture Locator">
            <Action name="FURNITURE_LOCATOR_TOGGLE">
                <Down>
                    if FurnitureLocatorDialogs then
                        FurnitureLocatorDialogs.ShowCategoryDialog()
                    end
                </Down>
            </Action>
        </Category>
    </Layer>
</Bindings>
